WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.942
XPath is a query language for selecting nodes and values from XML documents.

2
00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:06.242
In .

3
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:15.151
NET applications, it may appear in reporting, filtering, document routing, configuration lookup, identity workflows, or integration code.

4
00:00:15.151 --> 00:00:24.319
Because XPath controls what part of a document is selected, it should be treated as application logic rather than harmless string formatting.

5
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:31.147
A common design problem appears when user-controlled values are inserted directly into XPath expressions.

6
00:00:31.147 --> 00:00:43.112
If the input changes the meaning of the expression, the query can select data the developer did not intend or produce an error path that reveals more about the document than necessary.

7
00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:48.053
The defensive goal is to keep query structure controlled by the application.

8
00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:54.491
Prefer fixed expressions, allowlisted selectors, or mapping user choices to predefined expressions.

9
00:00:54.491 --> 00:01:03.074
For example, a user-facing option can select one of several known fields without allowing the user to provide the expression itself.

10
00:01:03.074 --> 00:01:13.283
When values must be compared, validate and encode them according to the API and design constraints rather than treating the expression as a free-form string.

11
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:23.752
Avoid using XML files as authorization databases unless the design has been reviewed for access control, query safety, document integrity, and update governance.

12
00:01:23.752 --> 00:01:32.140
It is easy for a simple XML lookup to become a policy decision without the protections expected from a real authorization system.

13
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.936
Error handling is part of the query design.

14
00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:45.796
XPath syntax failures and missing-node conditions should not expose sensitive document structure, protected values, internal paths, or full stack details to end users.

15
00:01:45.796 --> 00:01:53.989
Logs should identify the workflow and failure category while keeping sensitive XML content out of routine operational records.
